## 5. What Is Inheritance?

Inheritance is an object-oriented programming feature where one class receives attributes and methods from another class.

### Simple Definition

```text
Inheritance allows a subclass to reuse and extend the attributes and methods of a superclass.
```

### Example

```text
Superclass: Animal
Subclasses: Dog, Cat
```

Shared attributes:

```text
name
age
```

Shared methods:

```text
eat()
sleep()
```

Subclass-specific methods:

```text
Dog: bark()
Cat: meow()
```

### Mark Scheme Phrase

```text
Inheritance allows a subclass to inherit attributes and methods from a superclass, supporting code reuse and specialization.
```

---

## 6. Superclass and Subclass

### Superclass

A superclass is the general class.

```text
Animal
Vehicle
Person
Account
Shape
```

### Subclass

A subclass is a more specific class.

```text
Dog extends Animal
Car extends Vehicle
Student extends Person
SavingsAccount extends Account
Circle extends Shape
```

### Relationship

```text
subclass is a type of superclass
```

Example:

```text
A Dog is an Animal.
A Circle is a Shape.
```

---

## 7. Is-a Relationship

Inheritance should be used when there is an **is-a** relationship.

### Good Examples

```text
Dog is an Animal
Car is a Vehicle
Student is a Person
Circle is a Shape
SavingsAccount is an Account
```

### Bad Examples

```text
Car is an Engine
Student is a Course
Library is a Book
```

These are not inheritance relationships.

They are more likely composition:

```text
Car has an Engine
Student takes a Course
Library has Books
```

### Exam Phrase

```text
Inheritance is appropriate when the subclass is a more specific type of the superclass.
```

---

## 8. Inheritance Diagram

Simple class hierarchy:

```text
        Animal
       /      \
     Dog      Cat
```

Meaning:

```text
Dog extends Animal
Cat extends Animal
```

A `Dog` object has:

```text
Animal features
Dog-specific features
```

A `Cat` object has:

```text
Animal features
Cat-specific features
```

