## 27. Worked Example: Shape Polymorphism

### Superclass

```text
Shape
method: area()
```

Subclasses:

```text
Circle
Rectangle
Triangle
```

Each shape calculates area differently.

### Polymorphic Code Idea

```text
FOR each shape IN shapes
    OUTPUT shape.area()
ENDFOR
```

The same call:

```text
area()
```

runs different code depending on the actual shape.

### Exam Phrase

```text
Polymorphism allows a list of Shape objects to contain Circle and Rectangle objects, and calling area() uses the correct overridden method for each object.
```

