## 28. Worked Example: Game Characters

### Scenario

A game has different character types.

Superclass:

```text
Character
```

Subclasses:

```text
Warrior
Mage
Archer
```

Shared:

```text
name
health
move()
takeDamage()
```

Different:

```text
attack()
```

### Polymorphism

```text
character.attack()
```

could perform:

```text
Warrior: sword attack
Mage: spell attack
Archer: arrow attack
```

### Why Useful?

The game loop can call `attack()` without writing separate code for every character type.

