## 29. Common Design Mistakes

| Mistake | Why It Is Wrong | Better Design |
|---|---|---|
| using inheritance for has-a | wrong relationship | use composition |
| deep inheritance chain | hard to maintain | keep hierarchy simple |
| duplicated subclass code | misses superclass reuse | move shared code to superclass |
| overriding without same method signature | not true override | match method name/parameters |
| confusing overloading and overriding | wrong concept | overriding uses inherited method |
| making all attributes public | breaks encapsulation | use private/protected with methods |
| subclass depends too much on superclass internals | tight coupling | use clear superclass methods |
| no common method for polymorphism | cannot call shared method | define method in superclass/interface |
| using superclass when subclass-specific method needed | method may not be available | check variable type or design |
| assuming polymorphism means many classes only | incomplete | same method call, different behaviour |

